import ../../helpers/driver.dl
import ../../../ui/native.dl

window scroll test:
    label "Scroll input"

set state to 0
set instance to an instance of scroll test with state (the address of state)
set view to a UI view of (the address of instance) sized 640 by 480 using font "regular" with the test UI driver
set surface to a new native UI surface
set surface's view to the address of view
set graphics to a new DynlexGraphics
set graphics' application_state to (the address of surface) as a pointer
receive native UI scroll from ((the address of graphics) as a pointer) at 2.0 -3.0
require condition (view's input first's kind = 5) reporting "The graphics scroll resource did not reach the UI input queue"
require condition (view's input first's x = -80.0 and view's input first's y = 120.0) reporting "Native wheel offsets were not normalized to UI pixels"
process UI input in (the address of view)
require condition (view's input first = @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI input event)) reporting "The native scroll event was not consumed"
close the address of view
close the address of instance
print line "Native graphics scroll resources reach the UI as pixel offsets."
